# Letters: {{...}} marks words Claude added; everything else is Jimi's own wording from the source post.
L=[
dict(date="2026-11-24",slug="jesus-is-a-tomorrow-thinker",src=734,title="Jesus is a tomorrow thinker",body=[
"{{Look at}} what Jesus said to the woman caught in adultery:",
("“Then neither do I condemn you,” Jesus declared. “Go now and leave your life of sin.”","John 8:11"),
"Jesus is a tomorrow thinker. He is not so much concerned about your present as your future. He was saying {{to her}}: your past is over. I am not interested in your unworthy past. Stop looking back. I am your future.",
"When your past is over, your accuser will flee. The only thing that connects you to him is your past. He has no other information about you.",
"So do not look back, unless it is to thank God for what He has done. Discovery is for forward lookers. It is by looking forward that you find new things you would not ordinarily have dreamt of."],
pray="{{My}} past is over, {{Lord Jesus. You are my future. Amen.}}"),
dict(date="2026-11-25",slug="do-you-want-to-speak",src=1034,title="Do you want to speak? Pause a minute",body=[
"Think about what you said yesterday. Did your words build others up or pull them down? Did anyone benefit from them? Above all, did they glorify God?",
"If we are honest with ourselves, much of our conversation, prayer, fasting, preaching and teaching is nothing more than empty talk. God takes notice of every word we say, even the ones we ourselves do not notice.",
"God has entrusted you with a treasury. The heart is the treasury. The words are the things brought out of it.",
("“A good man brings good things out of the good stored up in him, and an evil man brings evil things out of the evil stored up in him.”","Matthew 12:35"),
"Love, kindness, tenderness, wisdom of utterance, the power to counsel. {{These}} are good treasures hidden in the heart, ready for use."],
pray="{{Lord, before I speak today, let me pause. Let my words come from the good You have stored in me. Amen.}}"),
dict(date="2026-11-26",slug="your-future-has-to-move-into-you",src=906,title="Your future has to move into you first",body=[
"Goliath’s dream was in his size, his weapons, his experience in warfare and his words of humiliation. Everyone could see it.",
"David was a small boy {{beside him}}. But he had a dream that was known to him alone.",
"Goliath looked at David from the human point of view. David looked at Goliath from God’s point of view.",
"Many look at their situation from the outside. On the outside it may be poor, painful and frightening. But remember your dream. That dream should be your focus, not your present situation. Your dream will impart strength to endure your present trials. If it is raining and you know the rain is only for a moment, you will endure. Trouble becomes easier to handle when you know it will not last.",
("“So we fix our eyes not on what is seen, but on what is unseen, since what is seen is temporary, but what is unseen is eternal.”","2 Corinthians 4:18"),
"Your future has to move into you before you can move into the future."],
pray="{{Lord, show me my situation from Your point of view. Let my future move into me today. Amen.}}"),
]

L+=[
dict(date="2026-11-27",slug="beyond-offence-there-god-is",src=785,title="Beyond offence, there God is",body=[
"Who has hurt you, today or in the past?",
"Imagine the deep hurt Joseph felt when his brothers tore his coat of many colours, threw him into a dry pit and left him for dead. He did not hold on to the offence. He let go of it, knowing that beyond offence, there God is. {{And God lifted him}} to the highest position {{in the land}}.",
("“For if you forgive other people when they sin against you, your heavenly Father will also forgive you.”","Matthew 6:14"),
"Many are asking for a blessing but have not let go of the grudge that is holding the blessing ransom. Like a bird suddenly caught in a trap, the devil lies in wait to catch you in the trap of offence.",
"Don’t remain a victim of self-imprisonment. Release yourself. {{Let go, and}} you will receive in a moment what you have been seeking for years."],
pray="{{I release them, and I}} release {{myself, in Jesus’ name. Amen.}}"),
dict(date="2026-11-28",slug="meditation-is-a-visit-with-him",src=799,title="Meditation in God’s Word is a visit with Him",body=[
"Enoch was great because his love for God was great.",
"How many times do you lovingly think about Jesus {{in a day}}? Many spend so much time thinking about their life partner, friends and possessions. Many are trying to climb the ladder of success. But the first place we are to prosper is in our spiritual life.",
("“But seek first his kingdom and his righteousness, and all these things will be given to you as well.”","Matthew 6:33"),
"If you are praying for a mighty blessing, you must first have a mighty relationship with God.",
"Meditation in God’s Word is a visit with Him. {{Visit Him today.}}"],
pray="I love You, Lord. {{Amen.}}"),
dict(date="2026-11-29",slug="the-weapon-of-testimony",src=488,title="The word of our testimony is a weapon",body=[
("“They triumphed over him by the blood of the Lamb and by the word of their testimony; they did not love their lives so much as to shrink from death.”","Revelation 12:11"),
"The word of our testimony is a weapon. We are meant to glorify God, not only for what He is doing now but for what He did in the past.",
"When people testify today, they talk about what God is doing now and forget what He did in the past. When you are faced with a new challenge, go down memory lane. If your situation is sickness, remember the sickness you had before and how God delivered you from the shackles of death.",
"At the grave of Lazarus, while people were crying and wailing, Jesus gave thanks to His Father. Lazarus was still in the grave. {{That was}} the weapon of testimony.",
"What is your situation? As long as God is aware of it, He will not leave you without a solution."],
pray="I am no longer condemned. I am what God says I am, I have what God says I have and I can do what God says I can do, in Jesus’ name. Amen."),
dict(date="2026-11-30",slug="gods-time-is-the-best",src=881,title="God’s time is the best",body=[
"When it is time to start a race, everybody waits for the sound of the gun. If any person beats the gun, that person is called back to begin afresh, while the others wait.",
"In our daily lives, the opposite is the case. We try to move the hands of the clock forward by hook and crook. To beat the gun, {{some}} kill, join cults, steal and destroy. And we pay dearly for it.",
"When His mother urged Him at the wedding, Jesus simply said, “My hour has not yet come.” He knew there is an appointed time for everything.",
("“There is a time for everything, and a season for every activity under the heavens.”","Ecclesiastes 3:1"),
"If you are in a haste to achieve something, you are likely to make costly mistakes that will pull you back, if not down. Always remember: God’s time is the best."],
pray="{{My times are in Your hands, Lord. I will not beat the gun. Amen.}}"),
]
